p_baby:
.str " NaN/0S  MANCHESTER SMALL-SCALE EXPERIMENTAL MACHINE - THE BABY - 21 JUNE 1948\n University of Manchester, England\n\n The first electronic stored-program computer. Program and data shared one\n electronic memory (Williams-Kilburn tube: 32 words x 32 bits) and a new\n program needed no rewiring. 7 instructions: JMP JRP LDN STO SUB CMP STP.\n\n THE PEOPLE\n   Freddie Williams  1911-1977  died   tube inventor, project lead\n   Tom Kilburn       1921-2001  died   wrote the first program\n   Geoff Tootill     1922-2017  died   built it, kept the notebook\n\n THE FIRST PROGRAM: highest proper factor of 2^18, trying 262143 downwards.\n Answer 131072 after about 52 minutes (~3.5 million store accesses).\n\n THIS EXHIBIT: exact machine (32x32-bit store, CI incremented before fetch).\n The program is a 20-instruction re-creation, not Kilburn's 17-instruction\n listing (TODO: transcribe it from Tootill's notebook for exact parity).\n\n [1] authentic run N=2^18 (3.4M Baby steps)   [2] quick run N=2^12   [ESC] back\n"
